WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.360
[LASER SOUNDS]

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.735
SPEAKER: Whether
you're exploring

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.630
a data set for the first
time or summarizing

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.250
the findings of your
analysis to an audience,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.160
you can use data visualization
to make large, complex data

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.270
sets easier to understand
and internalize.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.130
On this episode of
BigQuery Spotlight,

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.191
it's all about visualizing
your BigQuery data.

00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:21.039
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.940
Data visualization
is a tool that

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.360
helps you turn your complex
data into compelling stories,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.880
unlocking the insights that
both you and your audience

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.830
need to steer decision-making.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.540
Using dashboards or
infographics, for example,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.210
can help spark and
guide discussion

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.850
while the group explores
the data together.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.280
However, data
visualization is not just

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.510
for communicating
with decision makers.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.340
It is also an important part of
the exploratory analysis phase.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.250
Seeing data in visual form
helps you, as an analyst,

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.070
identify patterns,
outliers, trends,

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.630
or other interesting
data points you

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.220
want to investigate further.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.960
Choosing a data
visualization tool

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.350
comes down to
understanding your needs.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.970
First, consider your use case.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.210
Are you performing basic data
visualization and reporting?

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.420
Or more advanced tasks,
such as data modeling?

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.490
Secondly, you'll want
to balance the cost

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:17.120
of the tool against its feature
set and its learning curve.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.100
Fortunately,
BigQuery is connected

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.170
with several
visualization tools,

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.790
including those across
the partner ecosystem.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.450
So there's sure to be
one that's right for you.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.690
Today, we'll introduce two
of these tools, Data Studio

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.400
and Connected Sheets.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.100
Both give you the ability
to create quick, ad hoc data

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.320
visualizations, as well
as dashboards and reports.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.270
Let's take a closer
look at each one.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.890
First up, Data Studio, Google's
business intelligence and data

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:45.680
visualization platform that
lets you build scalable,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.320
serverless interactive
dashboards.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.820
Data Studio has two
main components.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.670
The first, Explorer,
is a place for you

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.620
to quickly derive
insights from your data

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.620
during the exploratory
phase of data analysis.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.020
It can be accessed
directly from BigQuery.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.200
Just click Explorer in Data
Studio from your query results

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.010
page.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.290
Data Studio will automatically
launch and create

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.137
a direct connection
to the query results.

00:02:09.137 --> 00:02:10.970
You'll land in the
Explorer interface, where

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.250
you can create quick
visualizations through drag

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.320
and drop functionality.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.490
On the back end, Data Studio
is creating SQL queries

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.740
in BigQuery to support your
exploration in real time.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.280
In fact, you can also use
Explorer with a BigQuery

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.140
table itself, rather
than query results,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.920
which means you don't need
to write any SQL at all.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.930
Just select the table
and click Export,

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.910
and choose Explorer
in Data Studio.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.740
The visuals you
create in Explorer

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:40.550
can be exported into the Reports
component of Data Studio.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.890
Data Studio Reports
provides a canvas

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.980
for bringing together visuals
into a dashboard, report,

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.480
or infographic.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.390
They're easy to share,
embed, and publish.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.730
Plus, you can make them
interactive for your viewer

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.730
by adding an option to filter,
or select a date range directly

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.380
in the live report.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.850
Data Studio is a great pick if
you want power with flexibility

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:02.600
and don't mind taking
a little bit of time

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.100
to get to know a new tool.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.470
Plus, it's available for free.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.290
If you're looking to wipe away
the learning curve pretty much

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.960
completely for you and
your collaborators,

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.960
you can do so with a second
tool, Connected Sheets.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.570
Connected Sheets allows you
to analyze and visualize

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.870
your BigQuery data, up
to billions of rows,

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.000
directly in a Google Sheet.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.680
So if you're a user
of Spreadsheets,

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.000
you already know all
you need to know.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.580
You can access
Connected Sheets right

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.010
from your BigQuery table
or your query results

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.590
by clicking Explore with Sheets.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.210
This will open up
a new Google Sheet

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.190
with a tab that has
a direct connection

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.690
to the full big query table.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.240
Your Connected Sheet
shows a preview

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.100
of the table, which
can be explored

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.650
by sorting and filtering.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.040
You can also reference the
connected Sheets in charts,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.230
pivot tables, and
functions, which

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:55.580
then use the entire BigQuery
table in its calculations.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.710
In order to support
these functions,

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:01.740
Connected Sheets runs queries
in BigQuery on your behalf.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.510
You can manually request the
query to run by hitting Apply.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.850
Results of those queries are
saved in your spreadsheet

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.920
for analysis and sharing.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.150
You can also schedule data
to refresh automatically.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.980
A quick note on availability.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.899
Connected Sheets is a
feature available only

00:04:17.899 --> 00:04:20.540
for G Suite Enterprise,
Enterprise for Education,

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.890
and Drive Enterprise
account customers.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.500
I also want to mention Looker--

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.710
a data platform which is
now part of Google Cloud.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.867
We recommend taking a
closer look at this tool,

00:04:29.867 --> 00:04:32.450
especially if you're seeking an
enterprise-ready solution that

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.600
delivers business intelligence
capabilities, powers

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.900
operational workflows with
data, and enables organizations

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.250
to build their own
data applications.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.120
There's a lot to learn in the
field of data visualization.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.740
As you gain experience,
you can learn

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.540
to create more
effective visuals,

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.550
use them to tell
compelling stories,

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.860
and fine tune your
design skills.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.570
And we hope that the
data visualization

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.130
tool will be just that--

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.790
a tool, and not any
additional mountain to climb.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.510
Try out Data Studio
and Connected

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:02.420
Sheets from your own
BigQuery sandbox project.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.550
You can connect one
of your own tables

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.830
or even a table from the
BigQuery public data sets

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.120
program.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.520
For a refresher on how to
set up your own sandbox

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.190
and access our public
data sets, follow the link

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.570
in the description below.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.460
If you want to learn
more about BigQuery,

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.987
check out the rest
of our playlist.

00:05:17.987 --> 00:05:19.820
And don't forget to
subscribe to our channel

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.680
on YouTube for
other great content.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.050
Look out for our next episode
of BigQuery Spotlight.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.830
And remember, stay curious.

